<title>USA: Dell cuts U.S. prices on Pentium PowerEdge.</title>
<headline>Dell cuts U.S. prices on Pentium PowerEdge.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dell Computer Corp said Wednesday it has cut prices between 22 percent and 41 percent on its entire line of Pentium PowerEdge network servers in the United States.</p>
<p>The company said it was able to reduce prices because it has been able to quickly pass on to customers the lower costs of components such as memory and processors.</p>
<p>Prices were reduced on all current Pentium PowerEdge systems, including SP, XE and XL models.</p>
</text>
